{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"## Per-alert verdict: all 5 are FALSE POSITIVES (dismissed with evidence)\n\nAnalysis done on origin/main at the time of the fix; all five reported line numbers\nmatched the current tip exactly (no drift from change 1630).\n\n### Alerts 86 / 87 — `_commands/_seam.py:452` (`screen_event`) and `:512` (`append_event`)\n\nFlagged expression at both sites: `\", \".join(data[\"secret_override\"][\"families\"])`.\n\n`data[\"secret_override\"]` is assigned two/three lines earlier from\n`rebar.secret_screen.override_record(findings, reason)`, which returns\n`{\"reason\", \"families\": sorted({f.family for f in findings}), \"locations\"}`.\n`SecretFinding.family` is a literal drawn from the module-level `SECRET_PATTERNS`\ntable in `src/rebar/secret_screen.py` — a fixed set of detector category names\n(\"Anthropic API key\", \"GitHub token\", ...). The `SecretFinding` dataclass carries only\n`family`/`field`/`line` and **structurally has no value field**; that is a documented,\ndeliberate property of the module (\"Report the family and the location, never the\nvalue\"), introduced by e7a9 precisely so reporting a leak cannot become a second leak.\n\nCodeQL taints the whole `data` payload — correctly, since it may carry a credential\nshape; that is what the screen just detected — and cannot see that this one key holds\nconstant category names. Taint over-approximation, not a leak.\n\n### Alerts 83 / 84 / 85 — `_commands/__init__.py:199`, `:204`, `:221`\n\nCodeQL's sensitive-data heuristic flags `_extract_allow_secret` on its NAME and taints\nits entire return tuple `(rest, reason)`, so plain argv (`rest`) inherits a \"secret\"\nlabel and all three downstream prints are reported. Two independent reasons this is\nfalse:\n\n1. The flagged value is the operator's free-text JUSTIFICATION for\n   `--allow-secret-pattern=<reason>` — not credential material at all.\n2. The flag token is *stripped* from `rest` before it is returned\n   (`if token.startswith(f\"{_ALLOW_SECRET_FLAG}=\"): reason = ...; continue`), so the\n   tainted value provably cannot reach any of the three prints.\n\nWhat is actually printed is `argv[0]` (an unknown command name), an unrecognised option\ntoken, and surplus positional arguments — the caller's own command line echoed back on\ntheir own stderr in a usage error.\n\n## Why no log-content change\n\nRedacting any of these would remove the diagnostic value — *which* detector was bypassed\non a forced write, *which* argument the CLI rejected — for zero security gain. No\nsecurity behaviour was weakened; the change is tests-only.\n\n## What was landed instead (Gerrit change 1671)\n\nRegression tests that PIN the invariant so a future edit cannot start logging the value:\n\n- `test_the_cli_forced_write_log_names_the_family_and_not_the_secret` — drives the CLI\n  forced-write route (`forced_secret_write` -> `screen_event`, the site of alert 86,\n  previously uncovered) with a synthetic credential and asserts the value plus its\n  12-char head and tail fragments are absent from captured log records, while the family\n  name is still present.\n- `test_usage_errors_never_echo_the_override_reason` — exercises all three usage-error\n  prints (alerts 83/84/85) with a sentinel `--allow-secret-pattern` value and asserts the\n  sentinel reaches neither stdout nor stderr, while each message still names the argument\n  it rejected.\n\nThe library forced-write route (alert 87) was already pinned by the pre-existing\n`test_force_override_lands_the_write_and_records_it_as_forced`.\n\nBoth new tests were verified **non-vacuous** by mutation: temporarily making\n`_seam.py:452` log the `data` payload and `__init__.py:199` append the override reason\nmakes each test fail with the expected assertion; restoring the sources makes them pass.\nAll 36 tests in the module pass; `make lint` and `make typecheck` are green.\n\n## Dismissal record\n\nAlerts 83, 84, 85, 86, 87 dismissed via\n`PATCH /repos/navapbc/rebar/code-scanning/alerts/<n>` with\n`state=dismissed`, `dismissed_reason=\"false positive\"` and a per-alert\n`dismissed_comment` carrying the evidence above (truncated to GitHub's 280-char cap and\npointing back to this ticket and change 1671). Verified afterwards:\n`gh api repos/navapbc/rebar/code-scanning/alerts --paginate` reports **0 open** alerts\nfor rule `py/clear-text-logging-sensitive-data`."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1786561551633899001,"uuid":"861d97f4-aa33-4f27-99a4-1fa6df40dae9"}